  "solution": "6 T # $ 4 B N 8 O P & + C V @ 1 2 M % * ? K 3 9 E \n\nLet's check each option:\n\n \n• @ **+ 1** = 1 and 1 **+ 2** = M\n\n __\n \n• \n \n6 T # $ 4 B N 8 O P & + C V ***@ 1 ***2*** M***__ % * ? K 3 9 E \n\n \n \n \n \n• \n \n* **+ 2** = K and K **+ 2** = 9\n\n __\n \n• \n \n​​​​​​​​6 T # $ 4 B N 8 O P & + C V @ 1 2 M % ******* ? ***K*** 3 ***9***__ E \n\n \n \n \n \n• \n \n​O **+ 1** = P and P **+ 2** = +\n\n __\n \n• \n \n​6 T # $ 4 B N 8 ***O P ***&*** +***__ C V @ 1 2 M % * ? K 3 9 E ​\n\n \n \n \n \n• \n \nT **+ 1** = # and # **+ 2** = 4\n\n __\n \n• \n \n​​6 ***T # ***$*** 4***__ B N 8 O P & + C V @ 1 2 M % * ? K 3 9 E​\n\n \n \n \n\nThus, here \"*K9\" is the odd one among the given options.\n\nHence, ‘*K9’ does not belong to the group.\n2f:Te42,\n<p style=\"",
